ath11k: give the NSS helpers internal linkage

Eleven functions added by the NSS patches in this series - the wifili
event and exception callbacks, the pdev init/start/deinit helpers, the
PPDU stats copy helpers and the AP arvif lookup - are called only from
the file that defines them, but were left with external linkage and no
prototype. ath11k_init()/ath11k_exit() are in the same state.

Mark them static. No behaviour change; it keeps symbols the NSS
offload path invents out of the module's global namespace and silences
the matching missing-prototype warnings.

The patch was previously called "add kernel 6_12", which described
nothing it does: none of its hunks is kernel-version dependent.

Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>

